IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `voca-dates`

-- Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 (Qld), Chapter 3 -- the victims financial assistance scheme.
-- SEAT-NEUTRAL CORE. The rules use the Act's own actors and terms: "the applicant", "a primary victim", "the scheme
-- manager", "the government assessor". The applicant's questions are in voca-seat.l4, which IMPORTs this module and
-- restates no rule. The Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 s 37(2)-(3) is in voca-mai-s37.l4.
--
-- PROVISIONS COVERED. s 5 (victim); ss 21, 23, 24 (the scheme; one capacity; death); ss 25, 25A, 25B (act of violence,
-- crime, series, as facts); s 26 (capacities); s 27 (injury); s 28 (exceptional circumstances, as a fact); Part 3 ss 31-34
-- (workers' compensation); Part 3A ss 36A-36F (motor accident claims); Part 3B ss 36G-36J (NIISQ, its facts as inputs);
-- Parts 4-8 ss 37-50 (amounts and components); Schedule 2 (special assistance); ss 51, 52, 54-61 (applying, time limits,
-- withdrawal, amendment, lapse); ss 78-82 (restrictions); ss 85, 86 (reductions); ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A (notifying a
-- relevant payment); ss 97-100 (interim assistance); s 101 (amending a grant); s 106G, s 123, s 126 (refunds);
-- ss 124-125 (review).
--
-- MONEY. Every amount and cap is in the Act or Schedule 2; no regulation under the Act is in force (README, Gaps).
-- "Reasonable" expenses are measured against the table of costs (s 132), which is not deposited: each expense is the
-- applicant's figure, taken as reasonable.
--
-- Edition: Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 (act-2009-035), the version in force from 2 September 2024 (current on
-- 20 October 2026), as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/act-2009-035.txt. An act of violence before 2 September
-- 2024 is `not covered`: chapters 6 and 8 to 10 carry transitional rules whose commencement days are not in the deposit.
--
-- BASELINE. Written with the writing-l4-rules skill, design defaults of 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Victims of Crime Assistance Act 2009 -- seat-neutral core`

§§ `The version covered`

-- The deposited version is in force from 2 September 2024, and chapters 8 to 10 (transitional provisions for the
-- amending Acts of 2017 and 2023) are in it, so those Acts had commenced by then. Chapter 9, s 220(2): "Chapter 3, as
-- amended by the amending Act, applies in relation to an act of violence only if the act is committed after the
-- commencement." The commencement days are not in the deposit, so an act of violence on or after 2 September 2024 is
-- the encoding's case, and an earlier act is `not covered`.
`the first day of the version encoded` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 2 9 2024

GIVEN `the day of the act of violence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act of violence is covered by this encoding` `the day of the act of violence` IF
    `the first day of the version encoded` `is on or before` `the day of the act of violence`

§§ `ss 25, 25A, 25B -- act of violence, crime, series`

-- s 25A(1): "A crime is an act or omission constituting a prescribed offence-- (a) disregarding any justification,
-- excuse or defence ...; and (b) whether or not the person who did the act ... has been identified, arrested, prosecuted
-- or convicted". (2): the disregarded defences do not include "a matter mentioned in the Criminal Code, section 31(1)(a)
-- or (b)" or "an authorisation to do an act or make an omission that is provided for under an Act". (3): "prescribed
-- offence means-- (a) an offence committed against the person of someone; or (b) an offence of attempting to commit, or
-- conspiring to commit, an offence mentioned in paragraph (a)."
-- s 25(1): "An act of violence is a crime or a series of related crimes ... that-- (a) are committed in Queensland; and
-- (b) directly result in the death of, or injury to, 1 or more persons, irrespective of where the death or injury
-- happened." (2): also "domestic violence, or a series of related acts of domestic violence," committed in Queensland
-- that directly results in death or injury. "Domestic violence" is the Domestic and Family Violence Protection Act 2012's
-- term (not deposited): a fact. A series (s 25B) "is taken to be a single act of violence" (s 25B(5)): a fact here.
DECLARE `What happened` HAS
    `was committed in Queensland`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `was an offence against the person of someone, or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was authorised under an Act, or done as mentioned in Criminal Code s 31(1)(a) or (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was domestic violence`                                                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `directly resulted in someone's death or injury`                                      IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a crime (s 25A)` `what happened` IF
        `what happened`'s `was an offence against the person of someone, or an attempt or conspiracy to commit one`
    AND NOT (`what happened`'s `was authorised under an Act, or done as mentioned in Criminal Code s 31(1)(a) or (b)`)

GIVEN `what happened` IS A `What happened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an act of violence (s 25)` `what happened` IF
        `what happened`'s `was committed in Queensland`
    AND `what happened`'s `directly resulted in someone's death or injury`
    AND (    `it is a crime (s 25A)` `what happened`
         OR  `what happened`'s `was domestic violence`)

§§ `s 27 -- injury`

-- s 27(1): "injury means-- (a) bodily injury; or (b) mental illness or disorder; or (c) intellectual impairment; or
-- (d) pregnancy; or (e) disease; or (f) for a sexual offence or domestic violence, the totality of the following adverse
-- impacts ... (i) sense of violation; (ii) reduced self worth or perception; ... (viii) adverse impact on feelings; or
-- (g) a combination". (2): "also includes an aggravation" of such an injury arising as a direct result of an act of
-- violence (only "to the extent of the effects of the aggravation", (3)).
DECLARE `Injury kinds` HAS
    `bodily injury`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `mental illness or disorder`                                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `intellectual impairment`                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `pregnancy`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `disease`                                                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the adverse impacts of a sexual offence or domestic violence in s 27(1)(f)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an aggravation of an injury of those kinds, caused by the act`     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `b` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`one if` `b` MEANS IF `b` THEN 1 ELSE 0

-- Schedule 2 s 1(3): "serious injury means an injury involving 2 or more of the kinds of injury mentioned in section
-- 27(1)(a) to (f)." An aggravation (s 27(2)) is not one of those kinds and is not counted.
GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury kinds`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of kinds in s 27(1)(a) to (f) in` `the injury` MEANS
      `one if` (`the injury`'s `bodily injury`)
    + `one if` (`the injury`'s `mental illness or disorder`)
    + `one if` (`the injury`'s `intellectual impairment`)
    + `one if` (`the injury`'s `pregnancy`)
    + `one if` (`the injury`'s `disease`)
    + `one if` (`the injury`'s `the adverse impacts of a sexual offence or domestic violence in s 27(1)(f)`)

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury kinds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an injury (s 27)` `the injury` IF
        `the number of kinds in s 27(1)(a) to (f) in` `the injury` AT LEAST 1
    OR  `the injury`'s `an aggravation of an injury of those kinds, caused by the act`

GIVEN `the injury` IS AN `Injury kinds`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a serious injury (Schedule 2)` `the injury` IF
    `the number of kinds in s 27(1)(a) to (f) in` `the injury` AT LEAST 2

§§ `s 5 -- victim (general meaning)`

-- s 5(1): "A victim is a person who has suffered harm-- (a) because a crime is committed against the person; or
-- (b) because the person is a family member or dependant of a person who has died or suffered harm because a crime is
-- committed against that person; or (c) as a direct result of intervening to help a person who has died or suffered
-- harm because a crime is committed against that person." (4): the person who commits the crime "is not a victim of the
-- crime under subsection (1)(b) or (c) or (3)". (5): the same for domestic violence. (2)-(3) (an unborn child's would-be
-- family member) are folded into the family member fact. Harm: "physical, mental or emotional harm" (Schedule 3).
-- For chapter 3, "victim" means "a primary victim, secondary victim or related victim" (Schedule 3, victim (b)).
DECLARE `Harm facts` HAS
    `suffered harm`                                                                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the crime or domestic violence was committed against them`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a family member or dependant of a person who died or was harmed by it`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `was harmed as a direct result of intervening to help a person who died or was harmed by it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed it`                                                                   IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Harm facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a victim within s 5` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `suffered harm`
    AND (    `the facts`'s `the crime or domestic violence was committed against them`
         OR  (    (    `the facts`'s `is a family member or dependant of a person who died or was harmed by it`
                   OR  `the facts`'s `was harmed as a direct result of intervening to help a person who died or was harmed by it`)
              AND NOT (`the facts`'s `committed it`)))

§§ `s 26 -- primary, secondary, parent secondary, witness secondary and related victims`

DECLARE `Victim capacity` IS ONE OF
    `primary victim`
    `parent secondary victim`
    `witness secondary victim`
    `related victim`

-- s 26(1): "A primary victim ... is a person who dies or is injured as a direct result of the act being committed against
-- the person." (3): "A parent secondary victim ... is a person who-- (a) is a parent of a child who is injured as a direct
-- result of the act being committed against the child; and (b) is injured as a direct result of becoming aware of the
-- act." (4): "A witness secondary victim ... is a person who is injured as a direct result of witnessing the act."
-- ("witness ... includes hearing the act or crime being committed", Schedule 3.) (5): "A related victim ... is a person
-- who is a close family member, or a dependant, of a primary victim of the act who has died as a direct result of the
-- act." (7): "close family member ... means a family member of the primary victim who had a genuine personal
-- relationship with the primary victim when the primary victim died." (6): "a person is not a victim of an act of
-- violence, of a kind mentioned in subsections (1) to (5), if the person committed the act."
DECLARE `Relationship to the act` HAS
    `was injured as a direct result of the act being committed against them`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a parent of a child injured as a direct result of the act being committed against the child` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was injured as a direct result of becoming aware of the act`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `was injured as a direct result of witnessing (seeing or hearing) the act`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `a primary victim of the act died as a direct result of it`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a family member of that primary victim with a genuine personal relationship with them when they died` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a dependant of that primary victim`                                                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed the act`                                                                     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to the act`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Victim capacity`
`the capacities under s 26 of` `the relationship` MEANS
    IF `the relationship`'s `committed the act`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE concat (LIST `primary`, `parent`, `witness`, `related`)
    WHERE
        `primary` MEANS
            IF `the relationship`'s `was injured as a direct result of the act being committed against them`
            THEN LIST `primary victim` ELSE EMPTY
        `parent` MEANS
            IF      `the relationship`'s `is a parent of a child injured as a direct result of the act being committed against the child`
                AND `the relationship`'s `was injured as a direct result of becoming aware of the act`
            THEN LIST `parent secondary victim` ELSE EMPTY
        `witness` MEANS
            IF `the relationship`'s `was injured as a direct result of witnessing (seeing or hearing) the act`
            THEN LIST `witness secondary victim` ELSE EMPTY
        `related` MEANS
            IF      `the relationship`'s `a primary victim of the act died as a direct result of it`
                AND (    `the relationship`'s `is a family member of that primary victim with a genuine personal relationship with them when they died`
                     OR  `the relationship`'s `is a dependant of that primary victim`)
            THEN LIST `related victim` ELSE EMPTY

-- s 23(1)-(2): a person who is a victim "in 2 or more of the following capacities-- (a) primary victim; (b) parent
-- secondary victim; (c) witness secondary victim; (d) related victim ... is eligible for victim assistance in relation
-- to the act of violence in only 1 of the capacities." The Act does not say which; s 60(2) lets the applicant change it.
-- ss 37, 40, 43, 47: each kind of victim "is eligible for assistance".
DECLARE `Capacity answer` IS ONE OF
    `no victim assistance: what happened is not an act of violence (ss 25, 25A)`
    `no victim assistance: a person who committed the act is not a victim of it (s 26(6))`
    `no victim assistance: a victim within s 5, but not a primary, secondary or related victim of the act (s 26)`
    `no victim assistance: not a victim of the act (ss 5, 26)`
    `eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` HAS `the capacities open` IS A LIST OF `Victim capacity`

GIVEN `what happened`    IS A `What happened`
      `the relationship` IS A `Relationship to the act`
      `the harm`         IS A `Harm facts`
GIVETH A `Capacity answer`
`the capacity answer for` `what happened` `the relationship` `the harm` MEANS
    IF NOT (`it is an act of violence (s 25)` `what happened`)
    THEN `no victim assistance: what happened is not an act of violence (ss 25, 25A)`
    ELSE IF `the relationship`'s `committed the act`
         THEN `no victim assistance: a person who committed the act is not a victim of it (s 26(6))`
         ELSE CONSIDER `the capacities under s 26 of` `the relationship`
              WHEN EMPTY THEN
                  IF `is a victim within s 5` `the harm`
                  THEN `no victim assistance: a victim within s 5, but not a primary, secondary or related victim of the act (s 26)`
                  ELSE `no victim assistance: not a victim of the act (ss 5, 26)`
              WHEN c FOLLOWED BY cs THEN `eligible for victim assistance, in only one of these capacities (ss 23, 37, 40, 43, 47)` (c FOLLOWED BY cs)

§§ `s 24 -- effect of death`

-- s 24: "(1) ... if a person entitled to assistance dies, the person's entitlement to assistance does not survive for
-- the benefit of the person's estate. (2) If a person applies for assistance but dies before the application is decided,
-- the application lapses. (3) If a person is granted assistance but dies before the assistance is paid to the person,
-- the assistance is taken to never have been granted and the person's application lapses."
DECLARE `Stage at death` IS ONE OF
    `entitled, but had not applied`
    `had applied, but the application was not decided`
    `had been granted assistance, not yet paid`
    `had been paid the assistance`

DECLARE `Death answer` IS ONE OF
    `the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
    `the application lapses (s 24(2)); the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
    `the assistance is taken never to have been granted, and the application lapses (s 24(3))`
    `s 24 says nothing about assistance already paid`

GIVEN `the stage` IS A `Stage at death`
GIVETH A `Death answer`
`the s 24 answer for` `the stage` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `entitled, but had not applied` THEN `the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
    WHEN `had applied, but the application was not decided` THEN `the application lapses (s 24(2)); the entitlement does not pass to the estate (s 24(1))`
    WHEN `had been granted assistance, not yet paid` THEN `the assistance is taken never to have been granted, and the application lapses (s 24(3))`
    WHEN `had been paid the assistance` THEN `s 24 says nothing about assistance already paid`

§§ `Schedule 2 -- special assistance (primary victims, s 39(h))`

DECLARE `Category` IS ONE OF `category A`, `category B`, `category C`, `category D`

-- Schedule 2 s 3, in its own order. Each item is the most serious thing the act of violence "involves"; the category is
-- the first list it appears in ("is not a category A act of violence and involves ..."). Criminal Code sections are
-- named by number only, as in the Schedule; the Code is not deposited. A sexual offence is "an offence of a sexual
-- nature" including rape, assault with intent to commit rape, and Criminal Code s 352 (Schedule 3); rape is listed in A.
DECLARE `What the act involved` IS ONE OF
    `attempted murder`
    `rape`
    `incest with a person under 16 or with an impaired capacity`
    `an act that constitutes an offence under Criminal Code s 229B`
    `an attempt to commit a category A act of violence`
    `a sexual offence other than rape`
    `grievous bodily harm`
    `an offence described in Criminal Code s 317`
    `robbery while armed or with personal violence or in company`
    `burglary with violence`
    `torture`
    `kidnapping`
    `an offence described in Criminal Code s 316`
    `domestic violence`
    `an attempt to commit a category B act of violence`
    `serious assault as described in Criminal Code s 340`
    `robbery`
    `unlawful wounding`
    `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company`
    `an offence described in Criminal Code s 364`
    `an attempt to commit a category C act of violence`
    `assault`
    `unlawful stalking, intimidation, harassment or abuse`
    `deprivation of liberty`
    `another act of violence not in category A, B or C`

GIVEN `the most serious` IS A `What the act involved`
GIVETH A `Category`
`the category (Schedule 2 s 3) of an act involving` `the most serious` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the most serious`
    WHEN `attempted murder` THEN `category A`
    WHEN `rape` THEN `category A`
    WHEN `incest with a person under 16 or with an impaired capacity` THEN `category A`
    WHEN `an act that constitutes an offence under Criminal Code s 229B` THEN `category A`
    WHEN `an attempt to commit a category A act of violence` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `a sexual offence other than rape` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `grievous bodily harm` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `an offence described in Criminal Code s 317` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `robbery while armed or with personal violence or in company` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `burglary with violence` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `torture` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `kidnapping` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `an offence described in Criminal Code s 316` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `domestic violence` THEN `category B`
    WHEN `an attempt to commit a category B act of violence` THEN `category C`
    WHEN `serious assault as described in Criminal Code s 340` THEN `category C`
    WHEN `robbery` THEN `category C`
    WHEN `unlawful wounding` THEN `category C`
    WHEN `assault occasioning bodily harm, including while armed or in company` THEN `category C`
    WHEN `an offence described in Criminal Code s 364` THEN `category C`
    OTHERWISE `category D`

-- Schedule 2 s 2: the table.
GIVEN `the category` IS A `Category`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special assistance for` `the category` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the category`
    WHEN `category A` THEN 15000
    WHEN `category B` THEN 9000
    WHEN `category C` THEN 6000
    WHEN `category D` THEN 3000

-- Schedule 2 s 1(3), "very serious injury": "(a) a bodily injury that-- (i) has resulted in a loss of a bodily function
-- (including a loss of capacity to have children), impairment of a bodily function ..., or disfigurement; and (ii) has
-- resulted in a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious; or (b) a bodily
-- injury that has resulted in the destruction of the life of an unborn child; or (c) a mental illness or disorder, or
-- intellectual impairment, that has resulted in a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is
-- otherwise very serious." Para 2: (a) and (c) are not very serious if the injury "would stop being very serious if it
-- were subjected to medical or other treatment". "very serious disease means a disease that is life threatening, and
-- includes human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)."
DECLARE `Special assistance facts` HAS
    `what the act involved, at its most serious`                                     IS A `What the act involved`
    `the act was a series of related crimes`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the injury`                                                                      IS AN `Injury kinds`
    `a bodily injury caused a loss or impairment of a bodily function, or disfigurement, and a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a mental illness or disorder, or intellectual impairment, caused a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that injury would stop being very serious if it were treated`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a bodily injury destroyed the life of the victim's unborn child`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `was infected with a life-threatening disease, such as HIV`                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `suffered a deprivation of liberty as a direct result of the act`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `was a child under 16 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was over 60 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `had an impaired capacity when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `suffered a very serious injury (Schedule 2)` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `a bodily injury destroyed the life of the victim's unborn child`
    OR  (    (    `the facts`'s `a bodily injury caused a loss or impairment of a bodily function, or disfigurement, and a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious`
              OR  `the facts`'s `a mental illness or disorder, or intellectual impairment, caused a permanent and significant reduction in quality of life or is otherwise very serious`)
         AND NOT (`the facts`'s `that injury would stop being very serious if it were treated`))

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was a child under 16, a person over 60 or a person with impaired capacity at the time` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `was a child under 16 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed`
    OR  `the facts`'s `was over 60 when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed`
    OR  `the facts`'s `had an impaired capacity when the act, or one of the acts in the series, was committed`

-- "category A circumstances, for a primary victim of a category B, C or D act of violence, means the victim has, as a
-- direct result of the act-- (a) suffered a very serious injury; or (b) been infected with a very serious disease."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `category A circumstances apply` `the facts` IF
        `suffered a very serious injury (Schedule 2)` `the facts`
    OR  `the facts`'s `was infected with a life-threatening disease, such as HIV`

-- "category B circumstances, for a primary victim of a category C or D act of violence, means-- (a) the victim has, as a
-- direct result of the act-- (i) suffered a serious injury; or (ii) been a victim of a series of related crimes; or
-- (iii) suffered a deprivation of liberty; and (b) when the act of violence was committed or, if the act of violence
-- involved a series of related crimes, when 1 or more of the acts were committed, the victim was-- (i) a child under
-- 16 years; or (ii) a person over 60 years; or (iii) a person with impaired capacity."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `category B circumstances apply` `the facts` IF
        (    `it is a serious injury (Schedule 2)` (`the facts`'s `the injury`)
         OR  `the facts`'s `the act was a series of related crimes`
         OR  `the facts`'s `suffered a deprivation of liberty as a direct result of the act`)
    AND `was a child under 16, a person over 60 or a person with impaired capacity at the time` `the facts`

-- "category C circumstances, for a primary victim of a category D act of violence, means-- (a) the victim has, as a
-- direct result of the act, been a victim of a series of related crimes; or (b) the act of violence does not involve a
-- series of related crimes and when the act of violence was committed, the victim was-- (i) a child under 16 years; or
-- (ii) a person over 60 years; or (iii) a person with impaired capacity."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `category C circumstances apply` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the act was a series of related crimes`
    OR  (    NOT (`the facts`'s `the act was a series of related crimes`)
         AND `was a child under 16, a person over 60 or a person with impaired capacity at the time` `the facts`)

-- Schedule 2 s 1(1): "(a) generally--the amount stated for the act in section 2 having regard to its category; (b) if the
-- act is a category B, C or D act of violence and category A circumstances apply ...--the amount stated in section 2 for
-- a category A act of violence; (c) if the act is a category C or D act of violence and category B circumstances apply
-- ...--... category B ...; (d) if the act is a category D act of violence and category C circumstances apply ...--...
-- category C". (2): for a series, "worked out, and is payable only, in relation to the act of violence in the series
-- that is of the highest category" -- the most serious item is the applicant's answer for the whole series.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A `Category`
`the category whose amount is paid (Schedule 2 s 1)` `the facts` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the category (Schedule 2 s 3) of an act involving` (`the facts`'s `what the act involved, at its most serious`)
    WHEN `category A` THEN `category A`
    WHEN `category B` THEN
        IF `category A circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category A` ELSE `category B`
    WHEN `category C` THEN
        IF `category A circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category A`
        ELSE IF `category B circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category B`
             ELSE `category C`
    WHEN `category D` THEN
        IF `category A circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category A`
        ELSE IF `category B circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category B`
             ELSE IF `category C circumstances apply` `the facts` THEN `category C`
                  ELSE `category D`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Special assistance facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special assistance payable (Schedule 2)` `the facts` MEANS
    `the special assistance for` (`the category whose amount is paid (Schedule 2 s 1)` `the facts`)

§§ `Parts 4 to 7 -- amount and composition of victim assistance; Part 3, s 32 -- workers' compensation`

-- Schedule 3: "more serious act of violence means an act of violence involving murder, unlawful striking causing death,
-- manslaughter or dangerous driving causing death"; "less serious act of violence means an act of violence that is not
-- a more serious act of violence". s 28 (exceptional circumstances) is the government assessor's judgment: a fact.
-- Expenses are the applicant's figures for expenses "incurred, or reasonably likely to be incurred" (s 29 "incurs":
-- paid, paid by someone else for the person, or invoiced), taken as reasonable against the table of costs (s 132).
DECLARE `Assistance claim` HAS
    `the capacity applied in`                                         IS A `Victim capacity`
    `the act is a more serious act of violence`                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `exceptional circumstances exist for the victim (s 28)`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `counselling expenses`                                            IS A NUMBER
    `medical expenses`                                                IS A NUMBER
    `incidental travel expenses`                                      IS A NUMBER
    `report expenses`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `loss of earnings in the 2 years`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `loss of or damage to clothing worn at the time`                  IS A NUMBER
    `other expenses to significantly help recovery`                   IS A NUMBER
    `what the primary victim would have given in the 2 years after death` IS A NUMBER
    `distress amount`                                                 IS A NUMBER
    `special assistance`                                              IS A NUMBER
    `funeral expense assistance granted to this victim for the act`  IS A NUMBER
    `legal costs of applying`                                         IS A NUMBER
    `is paid compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `lump sum compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`  IS A NUMBER
    `compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`           IS A NUMBER

-- ss 38(1), 41(1), 44(1), 48(1): the limits. "up to $120,000"; "up to $75,000"; witness: "(a) if the act is a more
-- serious act of violence--up to $75,000, less any funeral expense assistance granted to the victim for the act; or
-- (b) if the act is a less serious act of violence--up to $20,000, less any funeral expense assistance ..."; related:
-- "up to $75,000 less any funeral expense assistance granted to the victim in relation to the act".
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit on victim assistance for` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the capacity applied in`
    WHEN `primary victim` THEN 120000
    WHEN `parent secondary victim` THEN 75000
    WHEN `witness secondary victim` THEN
        IF `the claim`'s `the act is a more serious act of violence`
        THEN `not less than nothing` (75000 MINUS `the claim`'s `funeral expense assistance granted to this victim for the act`)
        ELSE `not less than nothing` (20000 MINUS `the claim`'s `funeral expense assistance granted to this victim for the act`)
    WHEN `related victim` THEN `not less than nothing` (75000 MINUS `the claim`'s `funeral expense assistance granted to this victim for the act`)

-- ss 38(2), 41(2), 44(2), 48(2): "up to $500 for legal costs incurred by the victim in applying for assistance". For a
-- witness, s 44(2) gives it only "In addition to the assistance mentioned in subsection (1)(a)" (a more serious act).
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the limit on legal costs for` `the claim` MEANS
    IF      `the claim`'s `the capacity applied in` EQUALS `witness secondary victim`
        AND NOT (`the claim`'s `the act is a more serious act of violence`)
    THEN 0
    ELSE 500

`the loss of earnings limit` MEANS 20000
`the limit for what the primary victim would have given` MEANS 20000
`the distress limit` MEANS 15000

GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim` MEANS
      `the claim`'s `counselling expenses`
    + `the claim`'s `medical expenses`
    + `the claim`'s `incidental travel expenses`
    + `the claim`'s `report expenses`

GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the loss of earnings component in` `the claim` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `loss of earnings in the 2 years`) `and` `the loss of earnings limit`

GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `exceptional circumstances exist for the victim (s 28)`
    THEN `the claim`'s `other expenses to significantly help recovery`
    ELSE 0

-- s 32(8): "non-expense assistance means the total amount of assistance for the components mentioned in section 49(e)
-- and (f)" -- s 49(e) "an amount of up to $20,000 that, but for the death of the primary victim ..., the related victim
-- would have been reasonably likely to receive from the primary victim, during a period of up to 2 years after the
-- primary victim's death"; (f) "an amount of up to $15,000 for distress".
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-expense assistance in` `the claim` MEANS
      `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `what the primary victim would have given in the 2 years after death`) `and` `the limit for what the primary victim would have given`
    + `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `distress amount`) `and` `the distress limit`

-- The components each Part allows, before the limit.
-- s 39 (primary): (a) counselling, (b) medical, (c) incidental travel, (d) report expenses; (e) "loss of earnings of up to
-- $20,000 ... during a period of up to 2 years after the act of violence"; (f) clothing the victim was wearing; (g) "if
-- exceptional circumstances exist for the victim, other reasonable expenses ... to significantly help the victim
-- recover"; (h) special assistance.
-- s 42 (parent secondary) and s 45 (witness, more serious act): (a)-(d); (e) loss of earnings up to $20,000 and (f) other
-- expenses, each only "if exceptional circumstances exist for the victim".
-- s 46 (witness, less serious act): (a)-(d) only.
-- s 49 (related): (a)-(d); (e) up to $20,000 of what the primary victim would have given; (f) up to $15,000 for distress;
-- (g) other expenses if exceptional circumstances exist.
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the components ordinarily payable in` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the capacity applied in`
    WHEN `primary victim` THEN
          `the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim`
        + `the loss of earnings component in` `the claim`
        + `the claim`'s `loss of or damage to clothing worn at the time`
        + `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`
        + `the claim`'s `special assistance`
    WHEN `parent secondary victim` THEN `the components for a secondary victim with exceptional earnings`
    WHEN `witness secondary victim` THEN
        IF `the claim`'s `the act is a more serious act of violence`
        THEN `the components for a secondary victim with exceptional earnings`
        ELSE `the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim`
    WHEN `related victim` THEN
          `the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim`
        + `the non-expense assistance in` `the claim`
        + `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`
    WHERE
        `the components for a secondary victim with exceptional earnings` MEANS
              `the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim`
            + (IF `the claim`'s `exceptional circumstances exist for the victim (s 28)`
               THEN `the loss of earnings component in` `the claim`
               ELSE 0)
            + `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`

-- s 31: Part 3 applies to "a primary victim, witness secondary victim or related victim" entitled to compensation under
-- the Workers' Compensation Act (the Workers' Compensation and Rehabilitation Act 2003). A parent secondary victim is not
-- in it. s 32(1): the section "states the assistance for which the person is eligible if the person is paid
-- compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act."
GIVEN `the capacity` IS A `Victim capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the capacity is one Part 3 applies to (s 31)` `the capacity` IF
        `the capacity` EQUALS `primary victim`
    OR  `the capacity` EQUALS `witness secondary victim`
    OR  `the capacity` EQUALS `related victim`

-- s 32(6), special assistance for a primary victim paid workers' compensation: "(a) if the person has not been paid any
-- lump sum compensation ...--special assistance of the amount that would ordinarily be payable ...; (b) if the person
-- has been paid lump sum compensation ... of an amount that is less than the amount of special assistance that would
-- ordinarily be payable ...--special assistance of the difference". A lump sum equal to or above the special
-- assistance leaves none: neither paragraph gives any.
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the special assistance under s 32(6) in` `the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `lump sum compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act` EQUALS 0
    THEN `the claim`'s `special assistance`
    ELSE IF `the claim`'s `lump sum compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act` LESS THAN `the claim`'s `special assistance`
         THEN `the claim`'s `special assistance` MINUS `the claim`'s `lump sum compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`
         ELSE 0

-- s 32(7), non-expense assistance for a related victim paid workers' compensation: "(a) only if the amount of the
-- compensation paid ... is less than the amount of the non-expense assistance that would ordinarily be payable ...; and
-- (b) only for the difference".
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the non-expense assistance under s 32(7) in` `the claim` MEANS
    IF `the claim`'s `compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act` LESS THAN `the non-expense assistance in` `the claim`
    THEN `the non-expense assistance in` `the claim` MINUS `the claim`'s `compensation paid under the Workers' Compensation Act`
    ELSE 0

-- s 32(2): a primary victim paid workers' compensation is eligible for "(a) assistance under section 38(1) for-- (i) the
-- components mentioned in section 39(f) and (g); and (ii) special assistance as mentioned in subsection (6); (b)
-- additional assistance under section 38(2)". (3): a witness to a more serious act, for "assistance under section
-- 44(1)(a) for the component mentioned in section 45(f)", s 44(2) and funeral expense assistance. (4): a witness to a
-- less serious act "is eligible for funeral expense assistance" only. (5): a related victim, for "the components
-- mentioned in section 49(a), (b), (c), (d) and (g)", non-expense assistance under (7), and s 48(2).
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the components payable in` `the claim` MEANS
    IF      `the claim`'s `is paid compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act`
        AND `the capacity is one Part 3 applies to (s 31)` (`the claim`'s `the capacity applied in`)
    THEN CONSIDER `the claim`'s `the capacity applied in`
         WHEN `primary victim` THEN
               `the claim`'s `loss of or damage to clothing worn at the time`
             + `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`
             + `the special assistance under s 32(6) in` `the claim`
         WHEN `witness secondary victim` THEN
             IF `the claim`'s `the act is a more serious act of violence`
             THEN `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`
             ELSE 0
         WHEN `related victim` THEN
               `the counselling, medical, travel and report expenses in` `the claim`
             + `the exceptional circumstances expenses in` `the claim`
             + `the non-expense assistance under s 32(7) in` `the claim`
         OTHERWISE `the components ordinarily payable in` `the claim`
    ELSE `the components ordinarily payable in` `the claim`

-- s 32(2)(b), (3)(b), (5)(b) keep the legal costs for a person paid workers' compensation; (4) does not.
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the legal costs payable in` `the claim` MEANS
    `the lesser of` (`the claim`'s `legal costs of applying`) `and` (`the limit on legal costs for` `the claim`)

-- The most that can be granted: the components, within the limit, plus legal costs within theirs.
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Assistance claim`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most victim assistance that can be granted for` `the claim` MEANS
      `the lesser of` (`the components payable in` `the claim`) `and` (`the limit on victim assistance for` `the claim`)
    + `the legal costs payable in` `the claim`

§§ `Part 8, s 50 -- funeral expense assistance`

-- s 50(1): a person "is eligible ... if the person incurs, or is reasonably likely to incur, funeral expenses for the
-- funeral of-- (a) a primary victim of an act of violence who dies as a direct result of the act; or (b) ... the unborn
-- child" of a pregnant primary victim whose life is destroyed as a direct result of the act. (2): not if "the person
-- committed the act of violence". (3): "up to $15,000 for funeral expenses ... for-- (a) ... each primary victim; or
-- (b) ... each unborn child". (4): "if more than 1 person is eligible ... only a combined total of up to $15,000 may be
-- granted to the persons for the funeral expenses for each primary victim or unborn child."
DECLARE `Funeral facts` HAS
    `incurs funeral expenses for a primary victim who died as a direct result of the act, or for an unborn child whose life it destroyed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed the act`                                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `the funeral expenses`                                                  IS A NUMBER
    `funeral expense assistance already granted to others for the same funeral` IS A NUMBER

`the funeral expense limit` MEANS 15000

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Funeral facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is eligible for funeral expense assistance (s 50(1)-(2))` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `incurs funeral expenses for a primary victim who died as a direct result of the act, or for an unborn child whose life it destroyed`
    AND NOT (`the facts`'s `committed the act`)

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Funeral facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most funeral expense assistance (s 50(3)-(4))` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `is eligible for funeral expense assistance (s 50(1)-(2))` `the facts`
    THEN `the lesser of` (`the facts`'s `the funeral expenses`) `and` (`not less than nothing` (`the funeral expense limit` MINUS `the facts`'s `funeral expense assistance already granted to others for the same funeral`))
    ELSE 0

§§ `Part 9 and Part 10 -- who may apply, the form, the time limits; Part 3, s 34`

-- s 51(1): "A victim ... may apply to the scheme manager". (2): for a child, "(a) the child's parent on behalf of the
-- child; or (b) if the child is at least 12 years old and is represented by a lawyer, the child; or (c) someone else
-- approved by the scheme manager." (4): for an adult with impaired capacity, "(a) if the victim has a guardian--the
-- guardian; or (b) if ... no guardian but has an administrator--the administrator; or (c) if ... neither--an attorney
-- appointed ... under an enduring power of attorney; or (d) if ... none of them--(i) a member of the victim's support
-- network; or (ii) someone else approved by the scheme manager." (5): another victim who "requires assistance in making
-- an application" -- someone else approved by the scheme manager. (6): "the victim is still the applicant".
DECLARE `Who may apply` IS ONE OF
    `the victim`
    `the child's parent, on the child's behalf`
    `the child, being at least 12 and represented by a lawyer`
    `someone else approved by the scheme manager`
    `the victim's guardian`
    `the victim's administrator`
    `the victim's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
    `a member of the victim's support network`

DECLARE `Applicant situation` HAS
    `is a child`                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `is at least 12`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `is represented by a lawyer`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an adult with an impaired capacity`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `has a guardian`                                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an administrator`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `has appointed an attorney under an enduring power of attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
    `needs help to make the application`                 IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the situation` IS AN `Applicant situation`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who may apply`
`who may make the application under s 51 for` `the situation` MEANS
    IF `the situation`'s `is a child`
    THEN IF `the situation`'s `is at least 12` AND `the situation`'s `is represented by a lawyer`
         THEN LIST `the child's parent, on the child's behalf`, `the child, being at least 12 and represented by a lawyer`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`
         ELSE LIST `the child's parent, on the child's behalf`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`
    ELSE IF `the situation`'s `is an adult with an impaired capacity`
         THEN IF `the situation`'s `has a guardian`
              THEN LIST `the victim's guardian`
              ELSE IF `the situation`'s `has an administrator`
                   THEN LIST `the victim's administrator`
                   ELSE IF `the situation`'s `has appointed an attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
                        THEN LIST `the victim's attorney under an enduring power of attorney`
                        ELSE LIST `a member of the victim's support network`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`
         ELSE IF `the situation`'s `needs help to make the application`
              THEN LIST `the victim`, `someone else approved by the scheme manager`
              ELSE LIST `the victim`

-- s 52: "An application for victim assistance must-- (a) be in the approved form; and (b) be accompanied by documents
-- supporting the application; and (c) contain the consent of the relevant person for the government assessor to obtain
-- information mentioned in section 74 or 77(1) or (4)." s 57: a funeral expense application "must be in the approved
-- form". s 55: victim and funeral applications on the same form "may" be considered together.
GIVEN `in the approved form`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `with supporting documents`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `with the consent to obtain information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the application meets s 52` `in the approved form` `with supporting documents` `with the consent to obtain information` IF
    `in the approved form` AND `with supporting documents` AND `with the consent to obtain information`

-- ss 59, 60: an applicant "may, by notice given to the scheme manager, withdraw [or amend] the application at any time
-- before the application is decided"; s 60(2) includes changing "the capacity in which the applicant is applying".
GIVEN `the application has been decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may withdraw or amend the application (ss 59, 60)` `the application has been decided` IF
    NOT `the application has been decided`

`the years to apply` MEANS 3

-- The facts that fix the last day to apply for victim assistance.
DECLARE `Application timing` HAS
    `the capacity applied in`                                     IS A `Victim capacity`
    `the day of the act of violence`                              IS A DATE
    `the day the primary victim died`                             IS A DATE
    `the victim's date of birth`                                  IS A DATE
    `is entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has made a workers' compensation application`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was finally dealt with`                           IS A DATE
    `has the scheme manager's approval under s 34(4)`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme manager has extended the time`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the time was extended to`                            IS A DATE

-- s 54(1): "within 3 years after-- (a) the act of violence happens; or (b) for an application by a related victim--the
-- death of the primary victim of the act; or (c) for a victim who is a child--the day the child turns 18." READING:
-- where more than one paragraph applies, the latest day is the limit; (c) applies to a victim who was a child when the
-- act happened. For a series of related crimes, (a) does not say which crime's day counts: the applicant's day is used.
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day under s 54(1) for` `the timing` MEANS
    `the later of the days` `the act or the death` `and` `the child's day`
    WHERE
        `three years after` MEANS
            GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
            YIELD `the day that is` `the years to apply` `years after` `d`
        `the act or the death` MEANS
            IF `the timing`'s `the capacity applied in` EQUALS `related victim`
            THEN `three years after` (`the later of the days` (`the timing`'s `the day of the act of violence`) `and` (`the timing`'s `the day the primary victim died`))
            ELSE `three years after` (`the timing`'s `the day of the act of violence`)
        `the child's day` MEANS
            IF `someone born on` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`) `is under` 18 `on` (`the timing`'s `the day of the act of violence`)
            THEN `three years after` (`the day someone born on` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`) `turns` 18)
            ELSE `three years after` (`the timing`'s `the day of the act of violence`)

-- s 34(1): a person in Part 3 "may apply for victim assistance ... only if-- (a) the person has made a workers'
-- compensation application; and (b) the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with." (2): "within 3
-- years after the person's workers' compensation application is finally dealt with; or (b) if the person is a child when
-- the person's workers' compensation application is finally dealt with--before the person turns 21." (3): "Subsection
-- (2) applies despite section 54(1)." (4): the scheme manager may approve an application "without first making a
-- workers' compensation application" (the prescribed period has passed, a waiver was refused, a reasonable excuse).
-- s 33: "finally dealt with when the person's total entitlement to compensation ... has been decided" (rejected, a lump
-- sum offer accepted or rejected, or the entitlement stopped): a fact.
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 34 governs when the person may apply` `the timing` IF
        `the capacity is one Part 3 applies to (s 31)` (`the timing`'s `the capacity applied in`)
    AND `the timing`'s `is entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act`
    AND NOT (`the timing`'s `has the scheme manager's approval under s 34(4)`)

GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may not apply yet (s 34(1))` `the timing` IF
        `s 34 governs when the person may apply` `the timing`
    AND NOT (    `the timing`'s `has made a workers' compensation application`
             AND `the timing`'s `the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with`)

GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day under s 34(2) for` `the timing` MEANS
    IF `someone born on` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`) `is under` 18 `on` (`the timing`'s `the day it was finally dealt with`)
    THEN `the later of the days` `three years on` `and` `the day before 21`
    ELSE `three years on`
    WHERE
        `three years on` MEANS `the day that is` `the years to apply` `years after` (`the timing`'s `the day it was finally dealt with`)
        `the day before 21` MEANS `the day that is` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the day someone born on` (`the timing`'s `the victim's date of birth`) `turns` 21)

-- s 54(2): the scheme manager "may, on application by a person, extend the time" (a judgment; the extended day is a
-- fact). READING: where s 34(4) approval is given, s 34(2) cannot run (there is no workers' compensation application),
-- so s 54(1) applies.
GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for victim assistance for` `the timing` MEANS
    IF `the timing`'s `the scheme manager has extended the time`
    THEN `the timing`'s `the day the time was extended to`
    ELSE IF `s 34 governs when the person may apply` `the timing`
         THEN `the last day under s 34(2) for` `the timing`
         ELSE `the last day under s 54(1) for` `the timing`

DECLARE `Time to apply answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: the last day to apply is` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `out of time: the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not yet: a workers' compensation application must first be made and finally dealt with (s 34(1)), unless the scheme manager approves under s 34(4)`
    `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`

GIVEN `the timing`       IS AN `Application timing`
      `the day of applying` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time to apply answer`
`the victim assistance time answer for` `the timing` `the day of applying` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the act of violence is covered by this encoding` (`the timing`'s `the day of the act of violence`))
    THEN `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
    ELSE IF `the person may not apply yet (s 34(1))` `the timing`
         THEN `not yet: a workers' compensation application must first be made and finally dealt with (s 34(1)), unless the scheme manager approves under s 34(4)`
         ELSE IF `the day of applying` `is on or before` (`the last day to apply for victim assistance for` `the timing`)
              THEN `in time: the last day to apply is` (`the last day to apply for victim assistance for` `the timing`)
              ELSE `out of time: the last day was` (`the last day to apply for victim assistance for` `the timing`)

-- s 58(1): "within-- (a) for a primary victim--3 years after the death of the victim; or (b) for an unborn child of a
-- primary victim--3 years after the life of the unborn child is destroyed." (2): the scheme manager may extend.
GIVEN `the day of the death`                     IS A DATE
      `the scheme manager has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the time was extended to`         IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply for funeral expense assistance` `the day of the death` `the scheme manager has extended the time` `the day the time was extended to` MEANS
    IF `the scheme manager has extended the time`
    THEN `the day the time was extended to`
    ELSE `the day that is` `the years to apply` `years after` `the day of the death`

GIVEN `the day of the act of violence`           IS A DATE
      `the day of the death`                     IS A DATE
      `the scheme manager has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the time was extended to`         IS A DATE
      `the day of applying`                      IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Time to apply answer`
`the funeral expense time answer for` `the day of the act of violence` `the day of the death` `the scheme manager has extended the time` `the day the time was extended to` `the day of applying` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the act of violence is covered by this encoding` `the day of the act of violence`)
    THEN `not covered: the act of violence happened before 2 September 2024, when transitional provisions not in the deposit may apply`
    ELSE IF `the day of applying` `is on or before` `the last day`
         THEN `in time: the last day to apply is` `the last day`
         ELSE `out of time: the last day was` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the last day to apply for funeral expense assistance` `the day of the death` `the scheme manager has extended the time` `the day the time was extended to`

§§ `Part 3A -- motor accident claims (with Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994 s 37 in voca-mai-s37.l4)`

-- s 36A: the Part applies if "(a) ... a person is a primary victim, secondary victim or related victim; and (b) the act
-- resulted in a motor vehicle accident within the meaning of the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994; and (c) the person
-- has made, or is or was entitled to make, a motor accident claim". s 36B: the person "may apply ... whether or not" a
-- claim has been made or finally dealt with. s 36C: "finally dealt with when ... (a) an insurer denies liability for the
-- claim; (b) an offer, or counter offer, of settlement of the claim is accepted; (c) a proceeding in a court based on the
-- claim ends, including any appeal."
DECLARE `Motor accident claim state` IS ONE OF
    `no motor accident claim has been made`
    `made, and not yet finally dealt with`
    `the insurer has denied liability for it`
    `an offer or counter offer of settlement has been accepted`
    `a court proceeding based on it has ended, including any appeal`

DECLARE `Motor accident facts` HAS
    `the act resulted in a motor vehicle accident (MAI s 4)`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `has made, or is or was entitled to make, a motor accident claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the claim`                                                 IS A `Motor accident claim state`
    `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)`                     IS A BOOLEAN
    `tried unsuccessfully under MAI s 37(3) to give late notice of the claim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the scheme manager is satisfied of a reasonable excuse for not claiming within the MAI s 37(2) period` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3A applies (s 36A)` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the act resulted in a motor vehicle accident (MAI s 4)`
    AND `the facts`'s `has made, or is or was entitled to make, a motor accident claim`

DECLARE `Motor accident deferral answer` IS ONE OF
    `Part 3A does not apply: no deferral for a motor accident claim`
    `no deferral: the motor accident claim has been finally dealt with (s 36C)`
    `no deferral: the claim is barred or late notice failed, and the scheme manager accepts my excuse (s 36D(3))`
    `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
    `deferred until my motor accident claim is finally dealt with (s 36E); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`

-- s 36D(2): where no claim has been made, "The government assessor must defer deciding the application until-- (a) the
-- applicant has made a motor accident claim ...; and (b) the claim has been finally dealt with." (3): not if the scheme
-- manager is satisfied "(a) that-- (i) a motor accident claim ... is barred under the Motor Accident Insurance Act 1994,
-- section 37(3); or (ii) the applicant has tried unsuccessfully under ... section 37(3) to give notice of a motor
-- accident claim ... after the period mentioned in section 37(2) of that Act; and (b) the applicant has a reasonable
-- excuse for not making the motor accident claim within the period mentioned in section 37(2)". s 36E(2): where a claim
-- is made but not finally dealt with, the assessor "must defer deciding the application until the motor accident claim
-- is finally dealt with." s 36F(2): "Despite the deferral ... must decide the application to the extent it relates to
-- assistance mentioned in section 39(a), 42(a), 45(a), 46(a) or 49(a)" (counselling expenses).
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Motor accident facts`
GIVETH A `Motor accident deferral answer`
`the Part 3A answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`Part 3A applies (s 36A)` `the facts`)
    THEN `Part 3A does not apply: no deferral for a motor accident claim`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the facts`'s `the claim`
         WHEN `no motor accident claim has been made` THEN
             IF      (    `the facts`'s `the claim is barred under MAI s 37(3)`
                      OR  `the facts`'s `tried unsuccessfully under MAI s 37(3) to give late notice of the claim`)
                 AND `the facts`'s `the scheme manager is satisfied of a reasonable excuse for not claiming within the MAI s 37(2) period`
             THEN `no deferral: the claim is barred or late notice failed, and the scheme manager accepts my excuse (s 36D(3))`
             ELSE `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
         WHEN `made, and not yet finally dealt with` THEN `deferred until my motor accident claim is finally dealt with (s 36E); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
         OTHERWISE `no deferral: the motor accident claim has been finally dealt with (s 36C)`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Motor accident deferral answer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the decision is deferred under s 36D or 36E` `the answer` IF
        `the answer` EQUALS `deferred until I make a motor accident claim and it is finally dealt with (s 36D(2)); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`
    OR  `the answer` EQUALS `deferred until my motor accident claim is finally dealt with (s 36E); counselling is decided now (s 36F)`

§§ `Part 3B -- the national injury insurance scheme (NIISQ facts as inputs)`

-- s 36G: the Part "applies to the primary victim ... if the primary victim or another person has made, or is entitled to
-- make, an application (an NIISQ application) under the NIISQ Act" (the National Injury Insurance Scheme (Queensland)
-- Act 2016, not deposited). s 36I(2): the government assessor "may defer deciding the application, or defer deciding the
-- amount of assistance ..., until the NIISQ application is decided." (3): if not decided "within 2 years after the
-- application was made, the government assessor must ... make the decision as soon as reasonably practicable." s 36J(2):
-- where s 36F does not apply, "Despite the deferral, the government assessor must decide the application to the extent
-- it relates to assistance mentioned in section 39(a) and (c) to (h)" -- everything but (b), medical expenses.
DECLARE `NIISQ facts` HAS
    `the capacity applied in`                                  IS A `Victim capacity`
    `an NIISQ application has been made, or can be made, for the injury` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the NIISQ application has been decided`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the decision is also deferred for a motor accident claim (s 36D or 36E)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the victim assistance application was made`       IS A DATE

DECLARE `NIISQ deferral answer` IS ONE OF
    `Part 3B does not apply: no deferral for an NIISQ application`
    `no deferral under s 36I: the NIISQ application has been decided`
    `the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); all but medical expenses is decided anyway (s 36J)` HAS `two years after applying` IS A DATE
    `the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); only counselling is decided anyway, because the motor accident deferral applies (s 36F)` HAS `two years after applying` IS A DATE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A `NIISQ facts`
GIVETH A `NIISQ deferral answer`
`the Part 3B answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF      NOT (`the facts`'s `the capacity applied in` EQUALS `primary victim`)
         OR NOT (`the facts`'s `an NIISQ application has been made, or can be made, for the injury`)
    THEN `Part 3B does not apply: no deferral for an NIISQ application`
    ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the NIISQ application has been decided`
         THEN `no deferral under s 36I: the NIISQ application has been decided`
         ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the decision is also deferred for a motor accident claim (s 36D or 36E)`
              THEN `the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); only counselling is decided anyway, because the motor accident deferral applies (s 36F)` `two years on`
              ELSE `the decision may wait for the NIISQ application, but after this day must be made as soon as reasonably practicable (s 36I); all but medical expenses is decided anyway (s 36J)` `two years on`
    WHERE
        `two years on` MEANS `the day that is` 2 `years after` (`the facts`'s `the day the victim assistance application was made`)

§§ `Part 3 -- may I apply yet, if I am entitled to workers' compensation (s 34)`

DECLARE `Workers' compensation answer` IS ONE OF
    `Part 3 does not apply: no workers' compensation condition on applying`
    `I may apply: my workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with (s 34(1))`
    `I may apply: the scheme manager has approved my applying without a workers' compensation application (s 34(4))`
    `not yet: I must first make a workers' compensation application (s 34(1)(a)), or, if its time has passed, ask the scheme manager for approval (s 34(4))`
    `not yet: I must wait until my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with (ss 33, 34(1)(b))`

GIVEN `the timing` IS AN `Application timing`
GIVETH A `Workers' compensation answer`
`the Part 3 answer for` `the timing` MEANS
    IF      NOT (`the capacity is one Part 3 applies to (s 31)` (`the timing`'s `the capacity applied in`))
         OR NOT (`the timing`'s `is entitled to compensation under the Workers' Compensation Act`)
    THEN `Part 3 does not apply: no workers' compensation condition on applying`
    ELSE IF `the timing`'s `has the scheme manager's approval under s 34(4)`
         THEN `I may apply: the scheme manager has approved my applying without a workers' compensation application (s 34(4))`
         ELSE IF NOT (`the timing`'s `has made a workers' compensation application`)
              THEN `not yet: I must first make a workers' compensation application (s 34(1)(a)), or, if its time has passed, ask the scheme manager for approval (s 34(4))`
              ELSE IF `the timing`'s `the workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with`
                   THEN `I may apply: my workers' compensation application has been finally dealt with (s 34(1))`
                   ELSE `not yet: I must wait until my workers' compensation application is finally dealt with (ss 33, 34(1)(b))`

§§ `Part 12, Division 3 -- restrictions on granting assistance (ss 78-82, with s 21(2)-(3))`

-- Each restriction turns on the government assessor being satisfied ("on the balance of probabilities", or "reasonably
-- satisfied"): the facts below are what the assessor would find.
DECLARE `Restriction facts` HAS
    `is eligible for the assistance under chapter 3`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `committed the act`                                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `conspired with the person who committed the act`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the primary victim`                                                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `the only or main reason the act was committed against the primary victim was the primary victim's involvement in a criminal activity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware of that involvement`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `was aware of it only because of witnessing the act`                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to a police officer`                                      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act was reported to the primary victim's counsellor, psychologist or doctor, or to a domestic violence service` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act involved a sexual offence or domestic violence`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the person who committed it was in a position of power, influence or trust in relation to the primary victim` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the primary victim was a child when it was committed, or has an impaired capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `there is a reasonable excuse for the act not being reported`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `did not give reasonable assistance in the police investigation`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the act is a crime or a series of related crimes`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `did not give reasonable assistance in the arrest or prosecution`               IS A BOOLEAN
    `that failure prevented the arrest or prosecution`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `had a reasonable excuse for not giving the assistance`                         IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 81(2): "special primary victim means-- (a) a primary victim of an act of violence-- (i) involving a sexual offence;
-- or (ii) committed by a person who was in a position of power, influence or trust in relation to the primary victim
-- ...; or (iii) involving domestic violence; or (b) a primary victim ... who-- (i) was a child when the act was
-- committed; or (ii) has an impaired capacity ...; or (c) a primary victim ... who is being threatened or intimidated".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Restriction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the primary victim is a special primary victim (s 81(2))` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the act involved a sexual offence or domestic violence`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the person who committed it was in a position of power, influence or trust in relation to the primary victim`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the primary victim was a child when it was committed, or has an impaired capacity`
    OR  `the facts`'s `the primary victim is being threatened or intimidated`

-- s 81(1): no grant if "(a) the act of violence has not been reported to-- (i) a police officer; or (ii) for an act of
-- violence against a special primary victim--a police officer, the victim's counsellor, psychologist or doctor, or a
-- domestic violence service; and (b) the government assessor is reasonably satisfied there is no reasonable excuse".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Restriction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the act counts as reported (s 81(1)(a))` `the facts` IF
        `the facts`'s `the act was reported to a police officer`
    OR  (    `the primary victim is a special primary victim (s 81(2))` `the facts`
         AND `the facts`'s `the act was reported to the primary victim's counsellor, psychologist or doctor, or to a domestic violence service`)

-- s 82(1): no grant if "(a) the person has not given reasonable assistance in-- (i) the police investigation (if any)
-- ...; or (ii) if the act ... is a crime or series of related crimes--the arrest or prosecution of the person who
-- committed, or allegedly committed, the act; and (b) if paragraph (a)(ii) applies--the failure has prevented the arrest
-- or prosecution". (2): "does not apply if the government assessor is reasonably satisfied the person had a reasonable
-- excuse".
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Restriction facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 82 bars the grant` `the facts` IF
        (    `the facts`'s `did not give reasonable assistance in the police investigation`
         OR  (    `the facts`'s `the act is a crime or a series of related crimes`
              AND `the facts`'s `did not give reasonable assistance in the arrest or prosecution`
              AND `the facts`'s `that failure prevented the arrest or prosecution`))
    AND NOT (`the facts`'s `had a reasonable excuse for not giving the assistance`)

DECLARE `Restriction answer` IS ONE OF
    `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`
    `no grant: not eligible for the assistance (s 78)`
    `no grant: committed or conspired to commit the act (ss 21(2)(a), 26(6), 79)`
    `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act (ss 21(2)(b), 80(1))`
    `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act, and I was or should have been aware of it (ss 21(2)(c), 80(2))`
    `no grant: the act was not reported, and there is no reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(a), 81)`
    `no grant: reasonable assistance was not given to the police investigation, or to an arrest or prosecution it prevented, without a reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(b), 82)`

-- s 78: "may grant assistance ... only if ... satisfied ... the person is eligible". s 79: "can not grant assistance to
-- a person if ... the person conspired with the person who committed the act of violence". s 80(1): no grant to a
-- primary victim if "the only reason, or the main reason, the act of violence was committed against the primary victim
-- was-- (a) because the victim was involved in a criminal activity when the act of violence happened; or (b) because of
-- the victim's previous involvement in a criminal activity". (2): no grant to "a person who is not the primary victim"
-- if that is so and "(b) the person was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware of the primary victim's involvement";
-- (3): "does not apply if the person was aware ... only because the person witnessed the act of violence."
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Restriction facts`
GIVETH A `Restriction answer`
`the restriction answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the facts`'s `is eligible for the assistance under chapter 3`)
    THEN `no grant: not eligible for the assistance (s 78)`
    ELSE IF `the facts`'s `committed the act` OR `the facts`'s `conspired with the person who committed the act`
         THEN `no grant: committed or conspired to commit the act (ss 21(2)(a), 26(6), 79)`
         ELSE IF `the facts`'s `is the primary victim` AND `the facts`'s `the only or main reason the act was committed against the primary victim was the primary victim's involvement in a criminal activity`
              THEN `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act (ss 21(2)(b), 80(1))`
              ELSE IF     (NOT (`the facts`'s `is the primary victim`))
                      AND `the facts`'s `the only or main reason the act was committed against the primary victim was the primary victim's involvement in a criminal activity`
                      AND `the facts`'s `was, or ought reasonably to have been, aware of that involvement`
                      AND NOT (`the facts`'s `was aware of it only because of witnessing the act`)
                   THEN `no grant: the primary victim's criminal activity was the only or main reason for the act, and I was or should have been aware of it (ss 21(2)(c), 80(2))`
                   ELSE IF     NOT (`the act counts as reported (s 81(1)(a))` `the facts`)
                           AND NOT (`the facts`'s `there is a reasonable excuse for the act not being reported`)
                        THEN `no grant: the act was not reported, and there is no reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(a), 81)`
                        ELSE IF `s 82 bars the grant` `the facts`
                             THEN `no grant: reasonable assistance was not given to the police investigation, or to an arrest or prosecution it prevented, without a reasonable excuse (ss 21(3)(b), 82)`
                             ELSE `nothing in ss 78 to 82 stops a grant`

§§ `Part 12, Division 5 -- working out the amount (ss 85, 86); Part 14, s 100 -- interim assistance deducted`

-- s 85(2): the government assessor "may reduce the amount that would otherwise be payable ... on the basis of ... (a)
-- the extent to which the applicant's conduct directly or indirectly contributed to the injury" -- the assessor's
-- judgment, an input percentage. (2)(b): no matter is prescribed (no regulation is in force).
-- s 86(2): "must reduce the amount of assistance that would otherwise be payable to the applicant by an amount
-- equivalent to the relevant payment." (2A): "does not apply to the extent the government assessor is satisfied the
-- purpose for which the relevant payment was or will be made does not include compensating the applicant for expenses
-- in relation to which the applicant is eligible for assistance."
-- READINGS: s 85 is applied first, then s 86; both to the amount after the limits ("would otherwise be payable").
GIVEN `the amount otherwise payable` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory conduct reduction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount after s 85` `the amount otherwise payable` `the contributory conduct reduction` MEANS
    `the amount otherwise payable` TIMES (1 MINUS `the contributory conduct reduction`)

GIVEN `the relevant payments` IS A NUMBER
      `the part made for another purpose` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 86 reduction for` `the relevant payments` `the part made for another purpose` MEANS
    `not less than nothing` (`the relevant payments` MINUS `the part made for another purpose`)

GIVEN `the amount otherwise payable`          IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory conduct reduction`    IS A NUMBER
      `the relevant payments`                 IS A NUMBER
      `the part made for another purpose`     IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assistance after ss 85 and 86` `the amount otherwise payable` `the contributory conduct reduction` `the relevant payments` `the part made for another purpose` MEANS
    `not less than nothing` ((`the amount after s 85` `the amount otherwise payable` `the contributory conduct reduction`) MINUS (`the s 86 reduction for` `the relevant payments` `the part made for another purpose`))

-- s 100(1)(a): "the amount paid in interim assistance must be deducted from the assistance otherwise payable".
GIVEN `the assistance granted` IS A NUMBER
      `the interim assistance paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the assistance still to be paid after interim assistance` `the assistance granted` `the interim assistance paid` MEANS
    `not less than nothing` (`the assistance granted` MINUS `the interim assistance paid`)

§§ `Part 14 -- interim assistance (ss 97-100)`

-- s 97: the Part applies if "(a) ... a person applies for assistance ... (general application); and (b) the government
-- assessor has not decided the general application; and (c) the person incurs, or is reasonably likely to incur before
-- the general application is decided, urgent and immediate expenses of a kind for which the person may be eligible for
-- assistance; and (d) in the general application, the person also applies for interim assistance". s 98(1): "may grant
-- ... assistance of up to $6,000 (interim assistance) for urgent or immediate expenses ... if the assessor is reasonably
-- satisfied it is necessary for the person to incur the expenses before the general application is decided."
DECLARE `Interim facts` HAS
    `has applied for victim or funeral expense assistance`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application has been decided`                                       IS A BOOLEAN
    `has urgent and immediate expenses before the decision, of a kind assistance can cover` IS A BOOLEAN
    `asked for interim assistance in the application`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the government assessor is reasonably satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the urgent expenses`                                                    IS A NUMBER

`the interim assistance limit` MEANS 6000

DECLARE `Interim answer` IS ONE OF
    `interim assistance can be granted, up to` HAS `dollars` IS A NUMBER
    `no interim assistance: Part 14 does not apply (s 97)`
    `no interim assistance: the government assessor is not satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision (s 98(1))`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Interim facts`
GIVETH A `Interim answer`
`the interim answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (    `the facts`'s `has applied for victim or funeral expense assistance`
            AND NOT (`the facts`'s `the application has been decided`)
            AND `the facts`'s `has urgent and immediate expenses before the decision, of a kind assistance can cover`
            AND `the facts`'s `asked for interim assistance in the application`)
    THEN `no interim assistance: Part 14 does not apply (s 97)`
    ELSE IF `the facts`'s `the government assessor is reasonably satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision`
         THEN `interim assistance can be granted, up to` (`the lesser of` (`the facts`'s `the urgent expenses`) `and` `the interim assistance limit`)
         ELSE `no interim assistance: the government assessor is not satisfied the expenses must be incurred before the decision (s 98(1))`

-- s 100(1)(b): "if the amount paid in interim assistance is more than the assistance payable in relation to the general
-- application--the person must refund the excess amount paid to the State." (2): "If the government assessor refuses the
-- person's general application ..., the person must refund the amount paid in interim assistance". (3): a debt.
GIVEN `the general application was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance granted`              IS A NUMBER
      `the interim assistance paid`         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the interim assistance to refund (s 100)` `the general application was refused` `the assistance granted` `the interim assistance paid` MEANS
    IF `the general application was refused`
    THEN `the interim assistance paid`
    ELSE `not less than nothing` (`the interim assistance paid` MINUS `the assistance granted`)

§§ `Part 11, s 61 -- lapse if no contact`

-- s 61(1)-(2): after 6 months without contact, the assessor "may give the applicant a notice stating that if the
-- applicant does not contact the government assessor within 6 months after the notice is given, the application will
-- lapse". (4): it then "lapses". (5): lapse "does not prevent the applicant making another application" (in time).
-- (6): contact with the scheme manager or another assessor acting for the one dealing with it counts.
`the months without contact` MEANS 6

DECLARE `Lapse answer` IS ONE OF
    `my application cannot lapse unless I am given a notice under s 61, which may be given after 6 months without contact`
    `my application stays open if I make contact by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `my application did not lapse: I made contact in time (s 61(4))`
    `my application has lapsed (s 61(4)); I may apply again within the time limit (s 61(5))`

GIVEN `a notice has been given`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice was given` IS A DATE
      `I have made contact since`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of contact, or today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Lapse answer`
`the s 61 answer for` `a notice has been given` `the day the notice was given` `I have made contact since` `the day of contact, or today` MEANS
    IF NOT `a notice has been given`
    THEN `my application cannot lapse unless I am given a notice under s 61, which may be given after 6 months without contact`
    ELSE IF `the day of contact, or today` `is on or before` `the last day`
         THEN IF `I have made contact since`
              THEN `my application did not lapse: I made contact in time (s 61(4))`
              ELSE `my application stays open if I make contact by` `the last day`
         ELSE `my application has lapsed (s 61(4)); I may apply again within the time limit (s 61(5))`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS `the day that is` `the months without contact` `months after` `the day the notice was given`

§§ `ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A -- telling the scheme manager about a relevant payment`

-- s 141A(2): an applicant who receives a relevant payment before the application is decided or interim assistance is
-- granted "must give the scheme manager written or oral notice of the relevant payment within 28 days after receiving
-- the payment, unless the applicant has a reasonable excuse" (maximum penalty 100 penalty units). s 98(2): the condition
-- on interim assistance, for a payment received "before the general application is decided". s 89(2): the condition on
-- every grant, for a payment received "within 6 years after the assistance is granted", notice "within 28 days after
-- receiving it". s 141B: contravening either condition without a reasonable excuse is an offence (100 penalty units).
-- "relevant payment" (Schedule 3): "any payment made or to be made to a person in relation to the act of violence whether
-- as damages, compensation, restitution, financial assistance, rebate, superannuation benefit, payment of an insurance
-- claim, or otherwise", including under the MAI Act, the Workers' Compensation Act, Medicare (Health Insurance Act 1973
-- (Cwlth) part 2), a superannuation scheme, an insurance policy and the NIISQ Act, but not a National Redress Scheme
-- payment.
DECLARE `Payment stage` IS ONE OF
    `before my application is decided and before any interim assistance is granted`
    `after interim assistance is granted, before my application is decided`
    `after assistance is granted`

`the days to notify a relevant payment` MEANS 28
`the years the s 89(2) condition runs` MEANS 6

GIVEN `the stage`                 IS A `Payment stage`
      `the day of the grant`      IS A DATE
      `the day of the payment`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty to notify the payment applies` `the stage` `the day of the grant` `the day of the payment` IF
    CONSIDER `the stage`
    WHEN `after assistance is granted` THEN `the day of the payment` `is on or before` (`the day that is` `the years the s 89(2) condition runs` `years after` `the day of the grant`)
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE `Payment notice answer` IS ONE OF
    `I must tell the scheme manager, in writing or orally, by` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no duty under ss 89(2), 98(2) or 141A: the payment came more than 6 years after the grant`

GIVEN `the stage`                 IS A `Payment stage`
      `the day of the grant`      IS A DATE
      `the day of the payment`    IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Payment notice answer`
`the payment notice answer for` `the stage` `the day of the grant` `the day of the payment` MEANS
    IF `the duty to notify the payment applies` `the stage` `the day of the grant` `the day of the payment`
    THEN `I must tell the scheme manager, in writing or orally, by` (`the day that is` `the days to notify a relevant payment` `days after` `the day of the payment`)
    ELSE `no duty under ss 89(2), 98(2) or 141A: the payment came more than 6 years after the grant`

§§ `Part 15, Division 1, s 101 -- applying to amend a grant`

-- s 101(1)-(2): a person granted assistance whose "circumstances have changed or are likely to change" may apply "to--
-- (a) change the amount of assistance granted; or (b) change the conditions" (not the s 89(2) condition). (3): "(a) if
-- the assistance was granted to an adult--within 6 years after the assistance was originally granted; or (b) if the
-- assistance was granted to a child--before the child turns 24." (5): "Only 1 application ... in a calendar year", but
-- (6) not if the scheme manager "is reasonably satisfied that exceptional circumstances exist", and (7) not if the person
-- "has been given an amendment notice under division 2".
DECLARE `Amendment facts` HAS
    `my circumstances have changed or are likely to change`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day assistance was originally granted`                  IS A DATE
    `my date of birth`                                           IS A DATE
    `the day of the amendment application`                       IS A DATE
    `applications to amend already made this calendar year`      IS A NUMBER
    `the scheme manager accepts exceptional circumstances for another this year` IS A BOOLEAN
    `I have been given an amendment notice under Division 2`     IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Amendment facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to apply to amend the grant (s 101(3))` `the facts` MEANS
    IF `someone born on` (`the facts`'s `my date of birth`) `is under` 18 `on` (`the facts`'s `the day assistance was originally granted`)
    THEN `the day that is` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the day someone born on` (`the facts`'s `my date of birth`) `turns` 24)
    ELSE `the day that is` 6 `years after` (`the facts`'s `the day assistance was originally granted`)

DECLARE `Amendment answer` IS ONE OF
    `I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: my circumstances have not changed and are not likely to (s 101(1)(b))`
    `no: out of time; the last day was` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `no: I have already applied this calendar year (s 101(5))`

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN `Amendment facts`
GIVETH A `Amendment answer`
`the s 101 answer for` `the facts` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the facts`'s `my circumstances have changed or are likely to change`)
    THEN `no: my circumstances have not changed and are not likely to (s 101(1)(b))`
    ELSE IF NOT (`the facts`'s `the day of the amendment application` `is on or before` (`the last day to apply to amend the grant (s 101(3))` `the facts`))
         THEN `no: out of time; the last day was` (`the last day to apply to amend the grant (s 101(3))` `the facts`)
         ELSE IF     `the facts`'s `applications to amend already made this calendar year` AT LEAST 1
                 AND NOT (`the facts`'s `the scheme manager accepts exceptional circumstances for another this year`)
                 AND NOT (`the facts`'s `I have been given an amendment notice under Division 2`)
              THEN `no: I have already applied this calendar year (s 101(5))`
              ELSE `I may apply to amend my grant, up to and including` (`the last day to apply to amend the grant (s 101(3))` `the facts`)

§§ `Refunds -- ss 100, 106G, 123, 126`

-- s 106G(1): "If the grant of assistance is amended under this division, the person must refund to the State the amount
-- of assistance paid to the person in excess of the amount of assistance granted following the amendment." (2): a debt.
-- s 123(2): if, in the prosecution for a fraud offence about the application (s 121: s 141(1)-(2), Criminal Code s 408C
-- or 488), "the prosecuting agency proves the assistance was granted on the basis of the person's acts or omissions
-- constituting the offence", "The assistance is taken never to have been granted and the person must refund to the
-- State any amount of the assistance paid". (4): "Any part ... not paid ... stops being payable". s 122: an undecided
-- application lapses. s 126(2): after a review reduces the grant, "refund to the State the amount of assistance paid to
-- the person in excess of the amount of assistance granted following the review."
DECLARE `Refund reason` IS ONE OF
    `interim assistance was more than my grant, or my application was refused (s 100)`
    `my grant was amended for an uncounted relevant payment (s 106G)`
    `I was convicted of a fraud offence about my application (s 123)`
    `my grant was reduced on review (s 126)`

GIVEN `the reason`                          IS A `Refund reason`
      `the amount paid to me`               IS A NUMBER
      `the assistance granted after`        IS A NUMBER
      `the application was refused`         IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecution proved the grant rested on the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the refund owed to the State for` `the reason` `the amount paid to me` `the assistance granted after` `the application was refused` `the prosecution proved the grant rested on the offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `interim assistance was more than my grant, or my application was refused (s 100)` THEN
        `the interim assistance to refund (s 100)` `the application was refused` `the assistance granted after` `the amount paid to me`
    WHEN `I was convicted of a fraud offence about my application (s 123)` THEN
        IF `the prosecution proved the grant rested on the offence` THEN `the amount paid to me` ELSE 0
    OTHERWISE `not less than nothing` (`the amount paid to me` MINUS `the assistance granted after`)

§§ `Part 18 -- internal and external review (ss 124, 125)`

-- s 124(1): "An applicant to whom a decision identified in schedule 1 applies may apply to the scheme manager for a
-- review". (2)(a): "within 28 days after the applicant is given notice of the decision". (3): "the scheme manager may, at
-- any time, extend the time". (4): applying "does not affect the operation of the decision". (8): "must be decided within
-- 42 days after it is made." s 125(2): after the internal review decision "The applicant may apply, as provided under
-- the QCAT Act, to QCAT for a review" (the QCAT Act, with its time limit, is not deposited).
`the days to apply for review` MEANS 28
`the days to decide a review` MEANS 42

DECLARE `Review answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: I can apply for internal review up to and including` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `out of time: the 28 days ended on` HAS `the last day` IS A DATE
    `not reviewable: the decision is not one identified in Schedule 1`

GIVEN `the decision is in Schedule 1`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was given notice`           IS A DATE
      `the scheme manager has extended the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the time was extended to`     IS A DATE
      `the day of applying`                  IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Review answer`
`the s 124 answer for` `the decision is in Schedule 1` `the day I was given notice` `the scheme manager has extended the time` `the day the time was extended to` `the day of applying` MEANS
    IF NOT `the decision is in Schedule 1`
    THEN `not reviewable: the decision is not one identified in Schedule 1`
    ELSE IF `the day of applying` `is on or before` `the last day`
         THEN `in time: I can apply for internal review up to and including` `the last day`
         ELSE `out of time: the 28 days ended on` `the last day`
    WHERE
        `the last day` MEANS
            IF `the scheme manager has extended the time`
            THEN `the day the time was extended to`
            ELSE `the day that is` `the days to apply for review` `days after` `the day I was given notice`

§§ `Regulative rules -- the applicant, the scheme manager and the government assessor`

-- Clock: days, counted from the day each rule starts (stated above each rule). The seat and the cases compute the
-- numbers from dates with the functions above.
DECLARE `VOCA party` IS ONE OF `the applicant`, `the scheme manager`, `the government assessor`

DECLARE `VOCA act` IS ONE OF
    `apply for victim assistance`
    `apply for funeral expense assistance`
    `contact the government assessor`
    `give the scheme manager notice of the relevant payment`
    `refund to the State` HAS `amount` IS A NUMBER
    `apply for internal review`
    `decide the review`

-- s 54(1) (or s 34(2), which "applies despite section 54(1)"): "An application for victim assistance ... must be made
-- within 3 years after ...". Day 0 is the day of the act of violence (for s 34(2), any fixed day before the last day);
-- the window is the number of days to the last day, which takes in a s 54(2) extension.
GIVEN `days to the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 54 -- the victim must apply for victim assistance within the time limit` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `apply for victim assistance`
    WITHIN `days to the last day`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 54(1) (s 34(2) for a person entitled to workers' compensation): the application for victim assistance was not made in time, and the scheme manager has not extended the time under s 54(2)"

-- s 58(1): "An application for funeral expense assistance must be made within-- (a) for a primary victim--3 years after
-- the death of the victim; or (b) for an unborn child ...--3 years after the life of the unborn child is destroyed." Day 0
-- is the day of the death.
GIVEN `days to the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 58 -- funeral expense assistance must be applied for within 3 years of the death` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `apply for funeral expense assistance`
    WITHIN `days to the last day`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 58(1): the application for funeral expense assistance was not made within 3 years after the death, and the scheme manager has not extended the time under s 58(2)"

-- s 61(2), (4): after a lapse notice, "if the applicant does not contact the government assessor within 6 months after
-- the notice is given, the application will lapse". Day 0 is the day the notice is given.
GIVEN `days to the last day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 61 -- after a lapse notice, the applicant must contact the government assessor within 6 months` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `contact the government assessor`
    WITHIN `days to the last day`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 61(4): the applicant did not contact the government assessor within 6 months after the notice, so the application lapses (s 61(5): another application may be made in time)"

-- ss 141A(2), 98(2), 89(2): notice of a relevant payment "within 28 days after receiving" it. Day 0 is the day the
-- payment is received.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `ss 89(2), 98(2), 141A -- the applicant must tell the scheme manager of a relevant payment within 28 days` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `give the scheme manager notice of the relevant payment`
    WITHIN `the days to notify a relevant payment`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "s 141A(2) or the condition under s 89(2) or 98(2) (offence, s 141B): notice of the relevant payment was not given within 28 days after receiving it, and there is no reasonable excuse"

-- s 100(1)(b), (2): "the person must refund the excess amount paid to the State"; "must refund the amount paid in
-- interim assistance". s 106G(1), s 123(2), s 126(2): "must refund to the State". None sets a time: each amount "is a
-- debt owed to the State" (ss 100(3), 106G(2), 123(3), 126(3)), so the rule has no WITHIN and never breaches by time
-- alone. Day 0 is the day the refund falls due (the decision, the amendment, the conviction, the review).
GIVEN `the amount to refund` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `ss 100, 106G, 123, 126 -- the person must refund the amount to the State` IS
    IF `the amount to refund` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN PARTY `the applicant`
         MUST  `refund to the State` (EXACTLY `the amount to refund`)
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- s 124(2)(a): an application for review "must ... be made within 28 days after the applicant is given notice of the
-- decision" (or the time as extended, (3)); applying is optional, so the rule is DO ... LEST FULFILLED. (8): "must be
-- decided within 42 days after it is made" -- the reviewer's duty (the scheme manager, or the assessor or departmental
-- employee nominated, (5)). Day 0 is the day notice of the decision is given.
GIVEN `days to apply` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `VOCA party` `VOCA act`
DECIDE `s 124 -- an internal review applied for in time must be decided within 42 days` IS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    DO    `apply for internal review`
    WITHIN `days to apply`
    HENCE
        PARTY `the scheme manager`
        MUST  `decide the review`
        WITHIN `the days to decide a review`
        LEST  BREACH BY `the scheme manager` BECAUSE "s 124(8): an application for internal review must be decided within 42 days after it is made"
    LEST  FULFILLED
